# AppShell

> Lede 0.8.1's docs for AppShell, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/app-shell.md

A page layout: a skip link, one primary `<nav>` and a `<main>`, where the nav is a sidebar on wide screens and a floating GlassBar on narrow ones. It fits an app with three to five places, each a whole screen.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/app-shell @lede/page-header
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md), [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md) and [`glass-bar`](glass-bar.md). It adds [`page-header`](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/page-header.md) only because the example below imports it. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.8.1/app-shell.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { AppShell } from '@/components/lede/blocks/app-shell';
```

