## Props

Page layout: a skip link, a `<nav>` and `<main id="main">`. Wide screens get a sidebar, and narrow screens get the same places in a bottom GlassBar. CSS shows only one of the two navs at a time, so assistive tech meets exactly one "Primary" landmark.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `brand` (required) | `React.ReactNode` |  | Product name or wordmark, shown at the top of the sidebar. |
| `nav` (required) | `ShellNavItem[]` |  | Three to five places. Sidebar on wide screens, a floating GlassBar on narrow ones. |
| `current` (required) | `string` |  | The current place, marked with `aria-current="page"`. Its label also names `<main>`. |
| `navLabel` | `string` | `Primary` | Accessible name of the primary navigation. Default `'Primary'`. |
| `sidebarFooter` | `React.ReactNode` |  | Extra sidebar content under the nav, on wide screens only, such as a footer link. |
| `children` (required) | `React.ReactNode` |  |  |
| `className` | `string` |  |  |

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { AppShell } from '@/components/lede/blocks/app-shell';
import { PageHeader } from '@/components/lede/blocks/page-header';

const NAV = [
  { value: 'today', label: 'Today', href: '/' },
  { value: 'inbox', label: 'Inbox', href: '/inbox' },
  { value: 'settings', label: 'Settings', href: '/settings' },
];

// A sidebar on wide screens and a floating GlassBar on narrow ones; the page goes inside <main>.
export function Layout({ current }: { current: string }) {
  return (
    <AppShell brand="Daybook" nav={NAV} current={current}>
      <PageHeader title="Today" summary="2 decisions need you" focusOnMount={false} />
    </AppShell>
  );
}
```

Docs: [Blocks](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/blocks.md) and [Layouts](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/layouts.md).

